     "title": "A negative area?",
     "ask": "∫ from 0 to 2 x² dx = 8/3. What is ∫ from 0 to 2 (−x²) dx?",
     "opts": [
      "−8/3",
      "8/3",
      "0",
      "16/3"
     ],
     "after": "−8/3. The region has the same size, but it is below the axis, so the integral is negative.",
     "ref": "Example 2",
     "id": "g12.maths.u2.s2-3-4.1"
    },
    {
     "kind": "read",
     "step": "read",
     "title": "Area below the axis",
     "paras": [
      "If f(x) ≥ 0 on [a, b], the area is ∫ from a to b of f(x) dx.",
      "If f(x) ≤ 0 on [a, b], the area is −∫ from a to b of f(x) dx.",
      "If f changes sign, split at the x-intercepts and add the areas."
     ],
     "note": "The integral = (area above) − (area below).",
     "ref": "p.144–147",
     "id": "g12.maths.u2.s2-3-4.2"
    },
    {
     "kind": "name",
